/surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>How important is functional status as a predictor of service use by older people</article-title><source>Journal of Aging and Health</source><year>1990</year><volume>2</volume><fpage>439</fpage><lpage>461</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10107279</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1177/089826439000200402</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Doumit</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Nasser</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Elderly Residents in Lebanese Nursing Homes: Quality of Life and Wellbeing</article-title><source>International Journal of Health Care Quality Assurance, (forthcoming)</source></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bucks</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Ashworth</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Wilcock</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Siegfried</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Assessment of activities of daily living in dementia: A Daily Living Scale. Development of the Bristol Activities</article-title><source>Age and Ageing</source><year>1996</year><volume>25</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>120</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8670538</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1093/ageing/25.2.113</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Katz</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Ford</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Moskowitz</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The index of ADL: A standardized measure of biological and psychosocial function</article-title><sou